// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WORLD 4-4 — the maze castle
//
// Generated by tools/smb-gen-world4.mjs from the original's area data — see
// reference/smb-areas.json. Pipe columns and heights, hole widths, block rows,
// the staircases, the flagpole and the castle are the original's own numbers,
// not an approximation of them. Re-run the generator rather than editing by
// hand.
//
// DEVIATION, and the only real one in world 4: this is the first level whose
// LoopCmd objects (columns 76 and 140) actually mean something, and we cannot
// honour them yet.
//
// LoopCmdE is `rts` — the object renders nothing. The maze lives in
// ProcLoopCommand, which checks three parallel tables when the player reaches
// the page: LoopCmdWorldNumber, LoopCmdPageNumber and LoopCmdYPosition. For
// world 4 the entries are page 5 at Y $40 and page 9 at Y $b0, and the player
// must also be in state 0, on the ground. Take the wrong height and
// ExecGameLoopback sends you back FOUR PAGES. Our engine has no such trigger,
// so the geometry is faithful but the maze does not loop — you can simply walk
// through. Everything else, Bowser and the axe at 173 included, is the
// original's.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

